## Summary
This article explores David Bowie's insights on art, religion, and technology, focusing on his creation and retirement of alter egos like Ziggy Stardust. It illustrates how Bowie used conceptual personae to delve into identity and challenge traditional rock stardom.

## Key Points
- David Bowie employed alter egos, such as Ziggy Stardust, as a deliberate artistic tool to explore persona and stardom.
- His work transcended music, encompassing themes of art, religion, and technology as part of his creative wisdom.
- The article highlights Bowie's methodical approach to crafting and discarding personae to redefine cultural narratives.


